        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">Logic: The middle two digits of the first number are interchanged to get the second number.</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Now, For,</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">1101 : 1011</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">⇒ 1 (10) 1 → Interchange middle digits (1,0) → 1 (01) 1 = 1011.</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Similarly, for <span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">2125 : ?</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">⇒ 2 (12) 5</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">⇒ Interchange middle digits (1, 2) → 2 (21) 5</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">⇒ 2215</span></p>\n",
